{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"laplacianEigenpairs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","text":"Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SB","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of eigenpairs, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"name":"smallest"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The weight of the edge at each position."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"weight"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"tolerance"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under Throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"maxIterations"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and nonnegative, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"laplacianSpectrum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the Laplacian L (","type":"text"},{"code":"laplacianMatrix()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), k = ","type":"text"},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"Eigenpairs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/laplacianeigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxiterations:)-2jn68"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/laplacianEigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-2jn68"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lapl